{"kind":"report","text":"Ready for independent review at exact clean head 4489a7b87efc0d878040c89ec5e2cebe51526626 on branch request/unreachable-sequence-pane-current-main, replayed onto current main a106e0e89391748143ac669320e9563ffce962dc. The commit message now names the real transition with file and line evidence re-derived at this anchoring, and claims no more than was checked. c77f68b added the pane and mounted it (App.tsx line 7 imports RightRail, line 45 renders it; RightRail.tsx line 6 imports SequencePane, line 53 renders it); 57c01ce deleted the rail for the Work drawer and carried the pane over (App.tsx line 7 imports WorkDrawer, line 75 renders it; WorkDrawer.tsx line 7 imports SequencePane, line 106 renders it behind the \"Durable record\" tab at line 79); 746a226 removed that tab, its inspect state and the import at WorkDrawer.tsx line 7, which is where the pane lost its mount, and stranded statementWeight in the same stroke (at 746a226^ Stream.tsx imported it at line 4 and called it at line 311). All of those were re-verified with git show at this re-anchoring and none had drifted. Two claims had drifted and are corrected in the message rather than carried forward. The stranded imports in store.ts are four, not three: at b73c5e1 workSummary took a vocabulary parameter, main has since dropped it, and statementWeight is now the last reader of the Vocabulary type in that file. And the shipped JavaScript is no longer byte-identical to main's, so that claim is replaced by what is actually measurable: both builds transform the same 1692 modules, the bundle keeps its exact 325,271-byte length, its byte histogram and all 2,479 distinct string literals, and the whole difference is a reordering within one 34 KB span with the minified names there reassigned, which moves the content hash and renames the asset index-twflYmIj.js to index-CgYu4uQo.js. Main's own embed was confirmed reproducible here first, so that measurement is against a sound baseline. The stylesheet is still exactly 454 bytes smaller, and the six utilities it loses are mx-2.5, w-20, border-l, bg-elevated/60, pl-2.5 and group-hover:inline. The deletion itself is unchanged in content. Conditions met: grep for SequencePane and statementWeight across ui/ returns nothing at this head; git merge-tree --write-tree main 4489a7b87efc0d878040c89ec5e2cebe51526626 exits 0 and writes tree e5c3e27ca47522f2fdadfaa3deaec2f3d0bd472e; UI suite 50 pass 0 fail; tsc exit 0; npm run build exit 0; make ui-check exit 0 against an embed regenerated by make ui and never hand-edited; make vet exit 0; make test exit 0 across all 15 packages with no wall-clock flake and no re-runs; git diff --check exit 0 both in the working tree and across main..HEAD. The worktree is clean at the pinned head and the commit carries its Rests-On trailer naming this request. Not merged and not ratified; independent exact-head review is requested from codex.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:dd119f574cbd547d3e996f2ebfd780d02950af02","branch":"request/unreachable-sequence-pane-current-main","commit_message":"Delete the sequence pane no reader could reach\n\nui/src/components/SequencePane.tsx and the statementWeight export in\nui/src/lib/store.ts are gone, along with the four imports in store.ts\nthat only they used. The pane was not stillborn. It was mounted when it\nwas written and orphaned later, and that history is worth stating\nexactly, because getting it wrong is the same error this deletion is\nabout.\n\nc77f68b, the chat-first redesign, added the pane and mounted it:\nui/src/App.tsx line 7 imports RightRail and line 45 renders it, while\nui/src/components/RightRail.tsx line 6 imports SequencePane and line 53\nrenders it. 57c01ce deleted the rail, replaced it with the Work drawer,\nand carried the pane over: App.tsx line 7 imports WorkDrawer and line 75\nrenders it, while ui/src/components/WorkDrawer.tsx line 7 imports\nSequencePane and line 106 renders it, behind a \"Durable record\" tab.\n746a226, \"Integrate and simplify the workroom UI\", removed that tab with\nits inspect state and the import at WorkDrawer.tsx line 7. That is where\nthe pane lost its mount.\n\nThe earlier version of this message claimed the pane was never mounted,\nbecause \"SequencePane\" never appears in ui/src/App.tsx. That proves only\nwhat App.tsx contains. Mounting is transitive through the component\ntree, and both real mount points were one file further down. A\nsingle-file grep cannot answer a reachability question, which is exactly\nthe question this change turns on.\n\n746a226 stranded statementWeight in the same stroke: at 746a226^,\nStream.tsx imported it at line 4 and called it at line 311; at 746a226\nits only occurrence in ui/ is its own declaration. Immediately before\nthis commit the whole repository held three references to the two\nsymbols — the two declarations and one test.\n\nThe four stranded imports are the Commitment and Vocabulary types from\n./api, workItemState from ./work, and definitionOf from ./util. Removing\ndefinitionOf empties the ./util import, so that line goes with it. The\ncount was three when this change was first written against b73c5e1;\nworkSummary took a vocabulary parameter there, and main has since\ndropped it, which leaves statementWeight as the last reader of\nVocabulary in this file.\n\nThat test is \"supersede provenance links are labeled neutrally on every\nsurface\". It read SequencePane.tsx, ThreadPane.tsx and Stream.tsx and\nrequired each to say \"linked item\" and never \"replacement\". It now reads\nthe two surfaces that ship. Nothing is lost: the pane's \"linked item\"\nline was unreachable, while ThreadPane's and Stream's are both on\nscreen.\n\nNo production JavaScript is added or removed. Both builds transform the\nsame 1692 modules, because rollup had already dropped both symbols from\nthe entry graph, and the bundle keeps its exact length of 325,271 bytes,\nits byte histogram, and all 2,479 of its distinct string literals.\nDropping the dead export nevertheless shifts rollup's emission order\nwithin one 34 KB span and reassigns the minified names it hands out\nthere, so the content hash moves and the asset is renamed from\nindex-twflYmIj.js to index-CgYu4uQo.js. The stylesheet is 454 bytes\nsmaller: Tailwind scans source files rather than the import graph, so\nsix utilities that only the pane used — mx-2.5, w-20, border-l,\nbg-elevated/60, pl-2.5 and group-hover:inline — are no longer generated.\nThe embed in internal/service/uidist is regenerated by make ui, not\nhand-edited.\n\nRests-On: git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:db90dd34a49dac59173c7a01796b0d5a412268e2","head":"4489a7b87efc0d878040c89ec5e2cebe51526626","main":"a106e0e89391748143ac669320e9563ffce962dc","merge_tree":"exit 0, tree e5c3e27ca47522f2fdadfaa3deaec2f3d0bd472e","status":"ready-for-review","tests":"UI suite 50 pass 0 fail; tsc exit 0; npm run build exit 0; make ui-check exit 0 (embed regenerated by make ui); make vet exit 0; make test exit 0 across 15 packages; git diff --check exit 0"}}